# InteractLab — Visualizations Section
## Implementation Plan + Claude Code Prompt

---

## 1. Purpose

Add a new top-level section to InteractLab: whiteboard-style, hand-drawn
animated walkthroughs of algorithm problems, synced with a code trace panel.
Same audience and hosting constraints as the rest of the site (mentor opens
it live in sessions, sometimes via `file://`, sometimes via GitHub Pages).

This section must follow the **exact same architectural rules** as
`week16-revision-app`, documented in CLAUDE.md. It is a new sibling folder,
not a modification of the existing app.

---

## 2. Non-negotiable constraints (carried over from CLAUDE.md)

- **No ES modules.** No `import`/`export`/`type="module"`. Everything is a
  plain `<script>` tag setting a `window.Foo` global. Reason: Chrome blocks
  ES module loading from `file://`, and the mentor sometimes double-clicks
  `index.html` directly.
- **No `DOMContentLoaded` wrapper.** Scripts load at the end of `<body>` in
  dependency order — the DOM is already parsed by then.
- **No template literals for multi-line code strings.** Use regular JS
  strings with `\n` escapes (this includes the `code` array of lines shown
  in the trace panel, and any Python snippets).
- **Content data lives separately from rendering logic** — problem data in
  `content/problems.js`, never inline in HTML or the engine file.
- **CDN-only for third-party libs**, loaded the same way CodeMirror/Pyodide
  already are — `<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/...">` before any
  inline script that uses the global it exposes.
- **Dark mode** inherited automatically via `site.css` variables — no new
  color system, reuse `--bg`, `--text`, `--teal`, `--purple`, `--amber`, etc.
- **Trace/step data is never hand-written.** It must be generated by running
  an instrumented version of the real algorithm and logging its state at
  each transition. This guarantees the animation can never desync from the
  actual logic.

