## 4. Data contract

`content/problems.js`:

```js
window.VIZ_PROBLEMS = [
  {
    id: 'smallest-window-sum',            // kebab-case, used as URL hash
    title: 'Smallest window >= target',
    difficulty: 'medium-hard',            // 'easy' | 'medium' | 'medium-hard'
    tags: ['Sliding Window', 'Arrays'],
    array: [2, 1, 5, 2, 3, 2],
    target: 7,
    code: [
      "def smallest_window(nums, target):",
      "    left = 0",
      "    current_sum = 0",
      "    min_len = float('inf')",
      "",
      "    for right in range(len(nums)):",
      "        current_sum += nums[right]",
      "",
      "        while current_sum >= target:",
      "            min_len = min(min_len, right - left + 1)",
      "            current_sum -= nums[left]",
      "            left += 1",
      "",
      "    return min_len"
    ],
    steps: [
      {
        left: 0,
        right: -1,
        sum: 0,
        minLen: null,
        codeLine: 1,
        narration: "Start with left pointer, running sum, and min_len at infinity."
      }
      // ...rest generated by tools/generate-trace.js
    ]
  }
];
```

`steps[]` fields are fixed: `left`, `right`, `sum`, `minLen` (null until a
window first qualifies), `codeLine` (0-indexed into `code[]`), `narration`
(plain string, whiteboard voice — simple English, no jargon, matches site
voice).

