## 5. Component responsibilities

### `viz-engine.js` — `window.VizEngine`
Constructor pattern, same as `window.FullIDE`:
```js
var viz = new window.VizEngine(mountEl, problemData);
viz.init();     // builds canvas, wires controls, renders step 0
viz.play();     // auto-advance with easing between steps
viz.pause();
viz.goTo(i);    // scrub to step i
viz.resize();   // re-measure container — same discipline as FullIDE.resize()
```
Internals:
- Canvas-based (not SVG DOM) rendering of array boxes, pointer arrows sliding
  with eased motion between step positions, and a synced code-line highlight.
- Sketchy/hand-drawn stroke style via `rough.js` (cdnjs), to get the
  whiteboard look.
- Narration text with typewriter reveal, timed to step transitions.
- Playback controller (play/pause/scrub/speed) is a **separate internal
  module from rendering** so future problem types can reuse it.

### `problem.html`
Reads the id from `location.hash`, looks it up in `window.VIZ_PROBLEMS`,
renders title/difficulty/tags, mounts `VizEngine`, and shows the full code
panel + narration below — same page shell pattern as the IDE tab (header +
tab context, not a bespoke layout).

### `visualizations/index.html`
Card grid over `window.VIZ_PROBLEMS`, styled like the Practice tab's problem
cards. Each card links to `problem.html#<id>`.

### `tools/generate-trace.js`
Node script. Takes an instrumented version of the target algorithm (you
write a small logging wrapper per problem), runs it, and emits a `steps[]`
array to paste into `content/problems.js`. This is the piece that must exist
**before** the first real problem's steps are authored — no hand-written
trace data, ever.

